Hi Avery,

Figma Make is now available to every seat on your plan.

Describe what you want ("a settings page with a plan selector and a billing history table"), and Make builds a working prototype using your design system's components and variables. Edit the result in Figma, or hand the code to engineering.

What's new since the beta:
- Uses your team library by default, so the output looks like your product
- Multi-screen flows with real navigation
- Export to a shareable prototype link or a code bundle
- Comments and version history, like any Figma file

Teams are using it for early concept reviews, customer-facing demos, and onboarding flows that used to need a sprint.

Try Make: https://mail.figma.com/l/make-ga-0922

